    "answer": {
      "short": "In column order $0^{\\circ},30^{\\circ},45^{\\circ},60^{\\circ},90^{\\circ}$:\n\n$\\sin\\theta$: $0,\\frac12,\\frac1{\\sqrt2},\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2},1$.\n\n$\\cos\\theta$: $1,\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2},\\frac1{\\sqrt2},\\frac12,0$.\n\n$\\tan\\theta$: $0,\\frac1{\\sqrt3},1,\\sqrt3$, undefined.",
      "worked": "Use the memorised exact-value table. In column order $0^{\\circ},30^{\\circ},45^{\\circ},60^{\\circ},90^{\\circ}$:\n\n$\\sin\\theta$: $0,\\frac12,\\frac1{\\sqrt2},\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2},1$.\n\n$\\cos\\theta$: $1,\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2},\\frac1{\\sqrt2},\\frac12,0$.\n\n$\\tan\\theta$: $0,\\frac1{\\sqrt3},1,\\sqrt3$, undefined.\n\nSince $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ and $\\cos90^{\\circ}=0$, $\\tan90^{\\circ}$ is undefined.",
